7	66	69	outright	/ˈaʊtˌɹaɪt/	adverb / adjective	Adverb: completely, openly, immediately, or without qualification. Adjective: complete, total, direct, or unambiguous.	completely, absolutely, flatly, categorically; total, complete, direct, unqualified	She rejected the proposal outright. / He denied the accusation outright. / That claim is an outright lie. / We bought the car outright rather than financing it.	Common combinations: reject/refuse/deny outright; outright ban/refusal/lie/victory. 'Buy/own outright' = without debt, installments, or shared ownership.		
