8	74	78	reconcile	/ˈɹɛ.kənˌsaɪl/	verb	1. To restore friendly relations between people. 2. To make two facts, accounts, statements, or positions consistent with each other. 3. To reconcile oneself to something: to accept an unpleasant reality.	make peace, reunite; harmonize, resolve, square, align; accept, come to terms with	They reconciled after years of tension. / We need to reconcile the two sets of figures before publishing the report. / She eventually reconciled herself to the fact that the plan had failed.	Three distinct grammar patterns: reconcile with someone; reconcile A with B; reconcile oneself to something. These are worth learning separately.		
