9	85	89	suffrage	/ˈsʌ.fɹɪdʒ/	noun	The legal or political right to vote in public elections.	voting rights, the franchise; enfranchisement (related process/state)	The movement campaigned for women's suffrage. / Universal suffrage means that adult citizens broadly have the right to vote. / Many activists fought for decades to secure suffrage.	'Ballot' is not a synonym: a ballot is the voting paper/process. 'Enfranchisement' is related but can mean the granting of voting rights, while suffrage is the right itself. Avoid the redundant phrase 'the right to suffrage'; say 'suffrage' or 'the right to vote'.		
