9	88	92	transpire / transpired	/tɹænˈspaɪɚd/	verb; often formal	1. To happen or occur. 2. To become known or be revealed, especially after being secret or unclear.	happen, occur, take place, unfold; emerge, come to light, become known	No one could believe what had transpired at the meeting. / It later transpired that the figures had been altered. / As more details transpired, the original story began to fall apart.	The 'happen' sense is standard in modern English, though older usage commentators sometimes objected to it. The 'become known' pattern is especially common in 'it transpired that...'.		
