10	91	95	unsustainably	/ˌʌn.səˈsteɪ.nə.bli/	adv	In a way, at a rate, or on a scale that cannot be maintained over the long term without exhausting resources, causing harm, or eventually failing.	at an unsustainable rate, nonviably, in a way that cannot be maintained (context-dependent)	The company was growing unsustainably fast and burning through cash. / Groundwater is being extracted unsustainably. / He had been working at an unsustainably intense pace for months.	'Excessively' and 'recklessly' may describe some cases but are not synonyms. The core idea is inability to continue over time. Common domains: environment, finance, growth, workload, debt, resource use.		
