12	119	124	foster / fostering	/ˈfɑ.stɚ.ɪŋ/	present participle of 'foster'	encouraging the development or growth of something	nurturing, promoting, cultivating	The school is committed to fostering creativity and independence.	Depth-pass addition: Prefer foster / fostering; foster growth/creativity/relations; also foster child/parent as adjective/noun-related family.		
