13	127	133	postulate	/ˈpɑs.tʃəˌleɪt/	verb / noun	Verb: to propose or assume something as a basis for reasoning, theory, or discussion, often without first proving it. Noun: an assumption or proposition accepted as a starting point for reasoning.	verb: posit, assume, hypothesize, propose; noun: assumption, premise, axiom (context-dependent)	The theory postulates that language ability has an innate component. / Euclidean geometry begins from a small set of postulates.	More formal and technical than ordinary 'suggest'. 'Postulate' emphasizes putting forward or accepting a proposition as a basis for further reasoning. An axiom/postulate distinction varies by field.		
