18	178	186	neurotransmitter	/ˈnʊr.oʊˌtræns.mɪ.tɚ/	noun	A chemical messenger released by a neuron that carries a signal across a synapse to another neuron, muscle cell, gland cell, or other target cell.	chemical messenger (descriptive); no exact simple synonym	Dopamine, serotonin, glutamate, and GABA are neurotransmitters with different roles in neural signaling.	'Synaptic agent' is not a standard synonym. Neurotransmitters are one part of neural communication; they should not be reduced to simplistic labels such as one chemical = one emotion or behavior.		
