26	256	267	public nuisance	/ˈpʌb.lɪk ˈnuː.səns	noun (law)	A condition, activity, or interference that unreasonably affects a right or interest shared by the public, with the precise legal test depending on jurisdiction.	public interference, community-wide nuisance (descriptive; no exact simple synonym)	The government argued that the illegal obstruction of the public waterway constituted a public nuisance.	Legal term; not every public annoyance or inconvenience is a public nuisance. Contrast private nuisance, which generally concerns interference with an individual's use or enjoyment of land. Rules and remedies vary by jurisdiction.		
