34	333	351	fable	/ˈfeɪ.bəl	noun	a short story, typically with animals as characters, conveying a moral	tale, parable, allegory	The fable of the tortoise and the hare teaches a lesson about perseverance.	Depth-pass guidance: Distinguish fable, parable, fairy tale, myth; also 'a fable' can mean false story.		
