36	353	372	demographic / demographics / demography / age group / age bracket	/ˌdɛm.əˈɡræf.ɪk eɪdʒ/	noun; adjective; comparison cluster	demographic (n.): a segment of a population, often defined by age or another characteristic; demographic (adj.): relating to population characteristics. demographics: statistical characteristics of a population or audience. demography: the study of populations and how their size/structure change. age group: people grouped by age; age bracket: a defined age range.	population segment, target group, age group, age bracket; population characteristics	Marketers often tailor ads to the 18–35 demographic. / People in the 18–35 age group were most likely to buy the product. / The survey divides respondents into several age brackets. / The demographics of the neighborhood have changed considerably. / Demography examines population structure and change, including age, births, deaths, and migration.	Replace unnatural 'demographic age'. Demographics may include age, sex/gender, income, education, race/ethnicity, location, household characteristics, etc., depending on context. 'Age demographic' is possible for a segment defined by age, but 'the 18–35 demographic', 'age group', or 'age bracket' is often more natural. 'Demographic data/trends/change' use demographic adjectivally.		
