36	356	376	gatekeeping / gatekeep	/ˈɡeɪtˌkiːp/	noun; verb (informal)	gatekeeping: controlling, restricting, or policing access to a community, identity, activity, information, or status, often by imposing unnecessary or exclusionary standards. gatekeep: to do this.	exclude, restrict access, police boundaries, control access; gatekeeper	There's a lot of gatekeeping in that fandom. / Stop gatekeeping anime. / He was gatekeeping the hobby by insisting that 'real fans' had to know every episode. / She gatekept the information for years. / Why is this information being gatekept?	Modern productive family: gatekeeping (very common noun/gerund), gatekeep (verb), gatekeeper (person/institution), gatekept (past/past participle). Hyphenated gate-keep is less usual in contemporary informal use. Gatekeeping can also have neutral institutional senses, e.g. editors or clinicians controlling access.		
