38	376	397	STEM vocabulary cluster: fields / disciplines / education / workforce / sector	/stɛm wɝːld/	noun phrase cluster	An umbrella cluster for talking naturally about science, technology, engineering, and mathematics as areas of study, education, employment, and industry.	STEM fields, STEM disciplines, STEM subjects, STEM education, STEM workforce, STEM careers/jobs, STEM professionals, STEM sector, STEM industries	She works in a STEM field. / Universities are trying to attract more students to STEM disciplines. / The program focuses on STEM education in middle schools. / Employers are competing for talent across the STEM workforce. / Women remain underrepresented in some STEM fields. / Investment in STEM industries has expanded rapidly.	Re-design weak headword 'STEM world' as an umbrella usage card. 'STEM world' is understandable and sometimes used informally, but field(s), disciplines, education, workforce, careers/jobs, professionals, sector/industries are usually more precise. Keep distinct from WID248 by focusing here on the broader vocabulary system, not just careers/jobs.		
