39	381	402	dismembering	/dɪsˈmɛmbərɪŋ/	verb	To disassemble or break apart a body or structure.	dissecting, separating	The criminal was dismembering the body in an abandoned house.	Depth-pass guidance: Normalize around dismember/dismemberment/dismembering. Cover literal removal of limbs/parts and figurative dismantling of territory/organization if appropriate; current crime example is unnecessarily graphic.		
