39	384	405	forebears	/ˈfɔːbɛərz/	noun (plural)	Ancestors or people of earlier generations, especially one's family or cultural predecessors.	ancestors, predecessors, progenitors	Our forebears built communities under much harsher conditions. / The tradition was passed down from our forebears.	Correct spelling is forebears. 'Forbears' is a form of the verb forbear (= refrain), so the current headword is a confusable spelling error.		
