39	386	407	AP class / AP course	/eɪ pi ˈklæs/	noun phrase	A high-school class or course in the U.S. Advanced Placement (AP) program, designed to offer college-level study and often prepare students for an AP exam.	Advanced Placement class, AP course	I'm taking three AP classes this year. / She took AP Biology and AP U.S. History in high school.	Capitalize AP. An AP class is the course itself, not 'a class of students'. AP exams are separate standardized exams associated with AP subjects.		
