55	550	581	rant	/rænt/	verb; noun	verb: to speak or complain at length in an angry, highly emotional, or forceful way. noun: a long angry or impassioned complaint or speech.	rail, rave, complain angrily; tirade, diatribe	He ranted about the new policy for twenty minutes. / Sorry for the rant—I needed to get that off my chest.	Fix current verb example ('went on a ranting spree') to natural patterns: rant about/against, go on a rant. A rant can be humorous/self-aware online, not always shouting.		
