56	559	591	pirouette / pirouetting	/ˈpɪrəˌwɛtɪŋ/	verb; noun	To spin on one foot or on the toes in ballet/dance; more loosely, to turn or spin gracefully. A pirouette is the turn itself.	spin, twirl, turn	The dancer pirouetted across the stage. / She performed three clean pirouettes. / Leaves were pirouetting in the wind.	Normalize to lemma. Figurative extension can describe graceful spinning motion outside dance.		
