61	607	640	sheep shearing	/ʃiːp ˈʃɛrɪŋ/	noun phrase	The process or event of cutting wool from sheep.	shearing, wool shearing	We visited a farm to watch a sheep-shearing demonstration. / Sheep shearing usually requires skill and proper handling.	Correct typo 'sheep sharing'. Shear (v.) → shearing (n./gerund). A person who shears sheep is a shearer.		
61	608	641	milenge (मिलेंगे)	/mɪˈlɛnɡeɪ/	Hindi expression / verb form	A Hindi form meaning roughly 'will meet'; in leave-taking expressions such as phir milenge, it conveys 'we'll meet again / see you again.'	see you again, we'll meet again (contextual translations)	Phir milenge! — See you again! / She ended the conversation with 'milenge,' using it as a casual leave-taking expression.	KEEP as source-language recognition card. More idiomatic leave-taking is often 'phir milenge' ('we'll meet again'). Romanization varies. Do not present isolated milenge as a universal one-word equivalent of goodbye.		
61	609	642	Psilocybe	/ˈsɪləsɪbi/	proper noun / genus name	A genus of fungi that includes species containing psilocybin as well as taxonomically related species; the term refers to the genus, not to psychedelic mushrooms as a generic common noun.	fungal genus; psilocybin-containing mushrooms (only for relevant species)	The paper examined several species in the genus Psilocybe. / Psilocybe cubensis is one well-known species in the genus.	Capitalize genus name and ideally italicize in scientific writing. Do not use 'Psilocybe' as an exact synonym for all 'magic mushrooms'; common labels cover multiple species/genera and taxonomic details matter.		
