62	611	644	misconstrue / misconstrued	/ˌmɪskənˈstruːd/	verb	To interpret or understand someone's words, actions, intentions, or a situation incorrectly.	misinterpret, misunderstand, misread, take the wrong way	Her friendliness was misconstrued as romantic interest. / Don't misconstrue my criticism as hostility.	Normalize lemma. Common pattern misconstrue A as B. Usually concerns mistaken interpretation, not deliberate distortion.		
62	612	645	garnish	/ˈɡɑrnɪʃ/	verb; noun	verb: to decorate or finish food/drink with an added item; noun: the decorative/flavoring item. In law/finance, garnish can also mean legally withhold money, especially wages, to satisfy a debt.	decorate, adorn; topping/accompaniment; withhold wages (legal)	Garnish the soup with chopped parsley. / Add a lemon twist as a garnish. / The court ordered his wages to be garnished.	Major missing legal/financial sense: garnish wages. Do not confuse with garnishee, a related legal term.		
