62	614	647	unfathomable	/ʌnˈfæðəməbəl/	adjective	Impossible or extremely difficult to understand, explain, measure, or imagine.	incomprehensible, inscrutable, inexplicable, unimaginable	Why he did it remains unfathomable to me. / The ocean once seemed unfathomable in both depth and mystery.	From fathom = measure depth / understand. Can intensify depth/scale metaphorically. Compare inscrutable: often motives/expressions that resist interpretation.		
