65	643	678	drive something home / drive the point home	/draɪv ˈsʌmθɪŋ hoʊm/	idiom	To make an idea, fact, warning, or lesson especially clear, forceful, or memorable through emphasis or evidence.	emphasize, underscore, reinforce, bring home	The photos drove home the scale of the disaster. / She repeated the figure to drive the point home.	Productive pattern drive home the point/fact/message/importance; pronoun/object variants possible. 'Bring something home to someone' is related but distinct.		
