65	646	681	evergreen	/ˈɛvɚˌɡriːn/	adjective; noun	noun: a plant that retains green foliage year-round. adjective: remaining useful, relevant, popular, or marketable over a long period; in media, 'evergreen content' stays timely.	perennial, enduring, timeless; evergreen plant	Pines are evergreens. / The site publishes evergreen articles that remain useful for years. / It's an evergreen favorite with audiences.	Strong media/business sense: evergreen content/topic. 'Evergreen classic' can be redundant depending context but is used. Perennial overlaps figuratively.		
