66	658	696	in disguise	/ɪn dɪsˈɡaɪz/	prepositional phrase	With one's identity or true nature concealed by changed appearance or presentation; figuratively, something appearing to be one thing while actually being another.	disguised, undercover, incognito; concealed	The detective entered the club in disguise. / The setback turned out to be a blessing in disguise.	Broaden beyond literal clothing. Related 'a blessing in disguise' is a fixed idiom. Incognito usually concerns concealing identity, not every disguised object/quality.		
