67	662	701	lozenge / lozenges	/ˈlɑzəndʒɪz/	noun	A small tablet or medicated sweet designed to dissolve slowly in the mouth, especially to soothe the throat; also a diamond/rhombus-shaped figure or object.	throat lozenge, cough drop, pastille; diamond shape (other sense)	I sucked on a throat lozenge to ease my sore throat. / The window was decorated with colored lozenge-shaped panes.	Normalize singular + plural. In everyday AmE, cough drop is often more natural for throat medication. Important second sense: a lozenge is a diamond/rhombus shape, especially in heraldry/design.		
