67	664	704	muscle spasm	/ˈmʌsəl ˈspæzəm/	noun phrase	A sudden involuntary tightening or contraction of a muscle; it may be brief or sustained and can range from painless twitching to painful cramping.	muscle contraction, cramp (some spasms), twitch (some cases)	I had a painful muscle spasm in my calf after the run. / Stress can sometimes trigger muscle spasms.	Do not equate every muscle spasm with a cramp: cramp is typically painful sustained contraction, while spasm is broader. Medical causes vary; card should remain vocabulary-focused, not diagnostic.		
