70	697	739	traverse / traversed	/trəˈvɝst/	verb; noun (specialist)	To travel, move, extend, or pass across or through an area; in technical contexts, to move across a structure, surface, network, or data structure.	cross, travel across, pass through, span	We traversed the valley before sunset. / The cable traverses the entire building. / The algorithm traverses the tree recursively.	Normalize lemma. More formal/technical than cross. Computing, climbing, surveying, and geography all use specialized senses.		
