74	735	777	tippy	/ˈtɪpi/	adjective (informal)	Easy to tip or overturn; unstable because of a high center of gravity or poor balance. In some informal contexts, it can also mean slightly unsteady, but that use is less standardized.	unstable, top-heavy, wobbly, easy to tip	That little table is too tippy for a heavy lamp. / The canoe felt tippy when I first got in.	Remove unsupported claim that it 'often' means mildly intoxicated. The robust sense is prone to tipping/unstable. For intoxication, tipsy is the standard word and a key confusable.		
