75	744	787	depravity	/dɪˈprævəti/	noun	Extreme moral corruption, wickedness, or degradation; the state or quality of being depraved.	wickedness, moral corruption, degeneracy, vice	The novel depicts both cruelty and human depravity. / Prosecutors described the crime in highly charged language about depravity.	Strong moralizing word, often used for severe wrongdoing. Related depraved. Avoid using casually for mere bad manners or ordinary flaws.		
75	745	788	rub off on someone	/rʌb ɔf ɑn ju/	phrasal verb / idiom	For a quality, habit, attitude, skill, or behavior to be gradually acquired from another person through contact or influence; literally, rub off = be removed by rubbing.	influence, transfer, be picked up, wear off (literal removal differs)	Her optimism is starting to rub off on me. / Spend enough time with him and some of his habits may rub off on you. / The ink rubbed off on my fingers.	Normalize from 'rub off on you'. Figurative pattern: X rubs off on someone. Literal rub off is separate and common.		
