75	748	791	apprehensive	/ˌæprɪˈhɛnsɪv/	adjective	Anxious, uneasy, or fearful about something that may happen in the future.	anxious, uneasy, nervous, worried, fearful	I was apprehensive about speaking in front of the whole group. / She felt apprehensive as the deadline approached.	Common: apprehensive about; apprehensive that... Usually anticipatory anxiety. Do not confuse with apprehend = understand/arrest.		
