76	754	797	truant	/ˈtruːənt/	noun; adjective	noun: a student who is absent from school without permission. adjective: absent without permission or neglecting a duty.	school absentee, absentee (broader), school-skipper (informal)	The school contacted the parents of repeated truants. / He was reported truant after missing several days without permission.	Related truancy. 'Truant' can be adjective: truant students. Absentee is broader and does not imply unauthorized absence.		
