80	798	850	slack	/slæk/	noun; adjective; verb	noun: looseness or unused capacity; adjective: loose/not taut or insufficiently active/strict; verb: to reduce effort or loosen. Common idioms include cut someone some slack and pick/take up the slack.	leeway, looseness, spare capacity; lax, loose	There's too much slack in the rope. / Sales are slack this month. / Cut her some slack—she's new. / When he left, the rest of us had to pick up the slack.	Highly polysemous. Do not reduce to 'freedom'. Productive idioms are important. Slack can also be a proper brand name, but that is separate.		
