81	801	853	rainbows and unicorns / all rainbows and unicorns	/ɔl ˈreɪnˌboʊz ənd ˈjuːnɪˌkɔrnz/	idiom (informal, often ironic)	An unrealistically cheerful, easy, idealized, or problem-free picture of reality; commonly used in negatives such as 'it's not all rainbows and unicorns.'	sunshine and rainbows, rosy picture, utopia (contextual)	Working for yourself isn't all rainbows and unicorns. / Her version of the story makes everything sound like rainbows and unicorns.	Normalize productive family. Usually ironic/sarcastic, especially 'not all...'. Related 'sunshine and rainbows'.		
