81	805	858	backslide / backsliding	/ˈbæksˌlaɪdɪŋ/	verb; noun	To return to a worse condition, former bad habit, lower standard, or abandoned belief after a period of improvement or reform; backsliding is the process/state.	relapse, regress, revert, fall back	I was exercising regularly, but I've started to backslide. / The report warns of democratic backsliding. / He worried about backsliding into old habits.	Normalize lemma. Strong modern collocations: democratic backsliding; backslide into old habits. Relapse is closer for illness/addiction and not exact everywhere.		
