84	831	885	contextual	/kənˈtɛkstʃuəl/	adjective	Relating to, depending on, or interpreted through the surrounding circumstances, information, language, culture, or situation.	context-dependent, situational, background-related	The meaning is highly contextual, so the isolated sentence is misleading. / The model uses contextual information from the surrounding text.	Common in language, analysis, AI, history. 'Contextual' does not merely mean 'related to background'; it often means meaning/behavior changes with context.		
