86	851	909	glib	/ɡlɪb/	adjective	Fluent, smooth, and confident in speech or explanation, but often too easy, superficial, insincere, or insufficiently thoughtful.	slick, facile, superficial, pat, smooth-talking	He gave a glib answer to a complicated ethical question. / Her glib charm worked at first, but people soon wanted specifics.	Usually disapproving. Glib does not merely mean fluent. Common: glib answer/explanation/remark; glib assurances.		
