86	856	914	hamstring	/ˈhæmˌstrɪŋ/	verb; noun	verb: to severely restrict, cripple, or prevent someone/something from functioning effectively; noun: one of the tendons/muscle group at the back of the thigh/knee region in everyday usage.	cripple, hinder, constrain, hobble	Budget cuts hamstrung the department. / The team was hamstrung by injuries. / He strained a hamstring during practice.	Major literal/anatomical + figurative family. Figurative passive 'be hamstrung by' is especially common.		
