86	859	917	hell or high water / come hell or high water	/hɛl ənd haɪ ˈwɑːtɚ/	idiom (informal)	No matter what difficulties or obstacles arise; despite severe trouble.	no matter what, whatever happens, at all costs, rain or shine	I'll finish this by Friday, come hell or high water. / She was determined to get there through hell or high water.	FIX headword: the established form is 'come hell or high water' (also 'through hell or high water'), not simply 'hell and high water'. Strong determination, often dramatic.		
