88	880	942	null / nulls	/nʌlz/	noun; adjective; verb (technical/general)	A null can be a zero, absence, empty/missing value, or point of zero response depending on the field; adjective null = having no legal force/value or no result; verb null is technical/rare outside computing.	zero, absence, missing value; void, invalid	The antenna pattern has several nulls where the signal drops sharply. / The database contains null values. / The contract was declared null and void.	Current definition is too narrow. Statistics, computing, engineering, law all use null differently. Do not equate database NULL with numeric zero.		
