96	956	1021	heuristic / heuristics	/hjʊˈrɪstɪks/	noun; adjective	A practical rule, shortcut, or strategy used to make judgments, solve problems, or search efficiently without guaranteeing an optimal or correct result; adjective: heuristic method/approach.	rule of thumb, shortcut, practical strategy	A simple heuristic can reduce the search space dramatically. / People often rely on heuristics when making quick judgments.	Normalize singular/plural and add adjective. Broader than 'mental shortcut': used in computer science, mathematics, design, decision-making. Heuristics trade certainty/optimality for speed or practicality.		
