99	981	1050	a fat lot of good / a fat lot of use / a fat lot of nothing	/fæt lɑt əv ˈnʌθɪŋ/	sarcastic idiomatic pattern (informal)	A sarcastic way to say that something is of little or no use, benefit, value, or quantity.	no use at all, no help, nothing worthwhile	A fat lot of good that umbrella did us in the storm. / We waited two hours and got a fat lot of nothing.	Broaden to the productive pattern. 'A fat lot of good/use' is especially established; 'fat lot of nothing' is possible and sarcastic. 'Fat lot' means very little, despite literal wording.		
