108	1072	1145	battery (law)	/ˈbætəri/	noun (law)	In many legal systems, intentional unlawful or offensive physical contact with another person; precise elements and the relationship to assault differ by jurisdiction.	unlawful touching, offensive contact; assault (not equivalent everywhere)	He was charged with battery after allegedly striking another man.	LEGAL PRECISION: definitions vary significantly by jurisdiction and between criminal law and tort law. Do not state that any unconsented contact automatically constitutes battery.		
108	1073	1146	consensual relationship	/kənˈsɛnʃuəl rɪˈleɪʃənʃɪp/	noun phrase	A relationship entered into voluntarily by the people involved, with mutual agreement to the relationship itself.	mutually agreed relationship, voluntary relationship	They described their relationship as consensual.	Important consent nuance: calling a relationship consensual does not imply blanket consent to every act within it. Consent remains specific, ongoing, and revocable.		
