110	1097	1171	foreboding	/fɔrˈboʊdɪŋ/	noun; adjective	noun: an uneasy feeling that something bad is going to happen. adjective: creating such a sense of threat or impending trouble.	dread, apprehension, premonition; ominous	I had a strange sense of foreboding. / The soundtrack creates a foreboding atmosphere.	Noun is especially common in 'a sense/feeling of foreboding'. Compare ominous = suggesting bad things are likely.		
