128	1279	1359	morose	/məˈroʊs/	adjective	Gloomy, sullen, withdrawn, and often noticeably bad-tempered or pessimistic.	gloomy, sullen, glum, dour	He became morose after the project fell apart and barely spoke at dinner.	Stronger and more literary/formal than sad. Often describes a person's mood, manner, expression, or temperament.		
