130	1295	1375	aggression	/əˈɡrɛʃən/	noun	Hostile, forceful, threatening, or attacking behavior; also forceful action by a state/group, and in psychology/behavior science, behavior intended to harm or dominate.	hostility, belligerence, attack, violence (context-dependent)	The dog's sudden aggression worried the owner. / The country condemned the act of aggression.	Not synonymous with violence in every context. 'Aggression' can be verbal, physical, strategic, or institutional; technical definitions vary by field.		
