133	1329	1411	bummed / bummed out	/bʌmd/	adjective (informal)	Disappointed, upset, or feeling low about something.	disappointed, down, upset, dejected	I was pretty bummed that the concert got canceled. / She was bummed out about missing the trip.	Usually means disappointed/down, not necessarily clinically depressed. Common patterns: bummed about/that; bummed out.		
133	1330	1412	goner	/ˈɡɔnɚ/	noun (informal)	A person or thing believed to be doomed, finished, beyond saving, or certain to fail/die.	doomed person/thing, lost cause, finished	When the car started sliding toward the cliff, I thought I was a goner. / That old laptop is a goner.	Can apply to objects as well as people. Often dramatic or humorous; 'dead meat' is more threatening and not a neutral synonym.		
