137	1362	1447	tout	/taʊtɪŋ/	verb; noun	verb: to praise, promote, recommend, or publicize something strongly; also to solicit business aggressively. noun: a person who solicits customers or sells tips, with senses varying by region/context.	promote, trumpet, advertise, praise; solicitor	The company touted the update as a major breakthrough. / Analysts are touting the stock as undervalued.	NORMALIZE from participle-only 'touting'. 'Tout' does not inherently mean overbearing or dishonest; context determines that. BrE has additional noun/verb senses around soliciting and ticket/scalping contexts.		
