144	1432	1518	jockstrap	ˈdʒɑkˌstræp	noun	A supportive undergarment for the male genitals, traditionally worn in sports; it may be used with a protective cup but does not itself necessarily provide impact protection.	athletic supporter, supporter	He wore a jockstrap under his uniform. / For contact sports, the supporter can hold a protective cup.	PRECISION: a jockstrap provides support; protection from impact generally comes from an inserted athletic cup. Avoid defining it as inherently protective.		
