150	1495	1583	spur-of-the-moment / on the spur of the moment	spɝː əv ðə ˈmoʊmənt	adjective / idiom	Done or decided suddenly, without advance planning; 'on the spur of the moment' = impulsively at that moment.	impromptu, spontaneous, unplanned, impulsive	It was a spur-of-the-moment decision. / We booked the trip on the spur of the moment.	Hyphenate before a noun: a spur-of-the-moment decision. This card overlaps an earlier family entry but remains useful as a form/collocation card.		
