150	1498	1586	Salisbury steak	ˈsɔːzbəri steɪk	noun	An American dish of seasoned ground beef formed into patties and typically served with gravy, often mushroom or onion gravy.	ground-beef patty dish	The diner served Salisbury steak with mashed potatoes and gravy.	Capitalize Salisbury. It is not literally steak cut from a whole muscle, and 'meatloaf steak' is not a standard synonym.		
