156	1557	1646	psyched	saɪkt	adjective (informal)	Very excited, enthusiastic, or eager about something.	excited, thrilled, pumped, stoked, amped	I'm psyched for the concert. / She's psyched about starting the new job.	Common patterns: psyched for/about/to do. Distinguish 'psyched up' = mentally prepared/energized and 'psyched out' = unnerved.		
