160	1591	1682	feel someone up	fiːl ʌp ˈsʌmwʌn	phrasal verb (slang, sexual)	To touch or grope someone's body sexually, especially breasts, buttocks, or genitals; often implies unwanted or inappropriate touching unless consensual context is explicit.	grope, fondle sexually	She said a stranger tried to feel her up on the crowded train.	NORMALIZE word order: feel someone up, not 'feel up someone'. Consent matters: the phrase is frequently used in allegations of unwanted touching, though consensual use is possible in context.		
