160	1597	1688	jaunty	ˈdʒɔːnti	adjective	Cheerful, lively, self-confident, and stylishly or casually spirited; also describing something set at a lively angle or with a brisk rhythm.	sprightly, breezy, lively, perky	He wore his hat at a jaunty angle. / The song has a jaunty rhythm.	Common collocations: jaunty angle, jaunty tune, jaunty walk. Can describe style/manner, not only mood.		
