161	1609	1700	shush	ʃʊʃ	interjection; verb	interjection: used to tell someone to be quiet. verb: to tell or cause someone to be quiet, often by saying 'shush'.	hush, quiet, silence	Shush! The movie's starting. / She shushed the kids when the announcement began.	Can be gentle/playful or sharp/rude depending tone. Unlike 'silence' as a verb, shush is distinctly informal.		
