162	1615	1706	neurotic	/nʊˈrɑtɪk/	adjective; noun (informal/dated person-label)	Characterized by excessive anxiety, worry, insecurity, or obsessive concern; historically related to 'neurosis', a broad older psychiatric category.	anxious, worried, obsessive, high-strung	I'm getting neurotic about checking whether I locked the door.	Modern everyday use is informal and can be judgmental; 'neurosis/neurotic disorder' has a complicated/dated psychiatric history. Avoid treating it as a precise diagnosis.		
162	1616	1707	perpendicular	/ˌpɝpənˈdɪkjəlɚ/	adjective; noun	At a right angle (90°) to a given line, plane, or surface; noun: a perpendicular line or direction.	at right angles, orthogonal (technical)	The two lines are perpendicular. / The pole is perpendicular to the ground.	CORRECTION: 'vertical/upright' are not general synonyms. A line can be perpendicular to another line without being vertical.		
