169	1682	1774	be my guest	/bi maɪ ɡɛst/	idiom	Used to give someone permission or invite them to do something; depending on tone, it can be warmly welcoming or dismissively mean 'go ahead if you insist'.	go ahead, feel free, help yourself	'Can I use your charger?' 'Be my guest.' / If you want to argue with him, be my guest.	Tone matters: polite permission vs ironic/dismissive challenge.		
