170	1694	1787	confidant / confidante	/ˈkɑnfɪˌdɑnt/	noun	A trusted person with whom one shares private thoughts, feelings, or secrets. 'Confidante' traditionally refers to a woman; 'confidant' is traditionally masculine but is now often used gender-neutrally.	trusted friend, trusted adviser	She became my closest confidante. / He was the president's longtime confidant.	Useful gender/form distinction. Pronunciation/spelling can be confused with 'confident' (adjective).		
