172	1716	1811	partisan	/ˈpɑrtəzən/	noun; adjective	noun: a committed supporter of a party, cause, or side. adjective: strongly supporting one side, often implying political bias or lack of neutrality.	supporter, adherent; biased, party-political	The proposal drew partisan opposition. / He was a loyal partisan of the movement.	Two POS. 'Partisan' need not mean irrationally biased, but adjective use often contrasts with bipartisan/nonpartisan. Also historical 'partisan' = guerrilla/resistance fighter in some contexts.		
