173	1728	1823	know squat about something / not know squat	/skwɑt əˈbaʊt ˈsʌmθɪŋ/	slang idiom	To know nothing or almost nothing about a subject. 'Squat' here means 'nothing' in informal negative constructions.	know nothing, know zilch, not know a thing	He doesn't know squat about fixing cars. / I know squat about tax law.	NORMALIZE: not 'squat about something' alone. Productive frame: 'don't/doesn't know squat about + topic'. Informal and mildly crude.		
