183	1824	1924	off-the-rack / off the rack	/ˌɔf ðə ˈræk/	adjective phrase; adverbial phrase	Ready-made in standard sizes rather than custom-made or made-to-measure, especially clothing; after a verb, often written 'off the rack'.	ready-to-wear, ready-made, non-custom	It's an off-the-rack suit. / I bought the suit off the rack.	KEY FORM: attributive adjective often hyphenated 'off-the-rack clothing'; after the verb, 'buy it off the rack'. Contrast bespoke/custom-made/made-to-measure.		
