183	1826	1926	at the thought of	/æt ðə θɔt əv/	prepositional phrase / collocation	When imagining, considering, or anticipating something; commonly introduces the trigger for an emotional or physical reaction.	at the idea of, just thinking about	She shuddered at the thought of going back. / My mouth waters at the thought of fresh bread.	KEY CONSTRUCTION: reaction verb/adjective + 'at the thought of + noun/gerund': shudder, cringe, smile, panic, feel sick, get excited at the thought of...		
