185	1846	1949	so + adjective + it hurts	/ðæt ɪz soʊ ˈaʊtˌdeɪtɪd ɪt hɝts/	productive hyperbolic construction	An informal exaggerating pattern meaning something has a quality to such an extreme degree that it is almost painful, embarrassing, or overwhelming; the source uses 'so outdated it hurts'.	painfully + adjective, extremely, ridiculously	That design is so outdated it hurts. / He's so talented it hurts.	KEY CONSTRUCTION: 'so + adjective + (that) it hurts'. Often humorous/hyperbolic; 'painfully outdated/obvious/awkward' expresses a similar idea.		
