185	1848	1951	Yoo-hoo	/ˈjuːˌhuː/	brand / proper noun	A U.S. chocolate-flavored beverage brand. It is marketed as a chocolate drink rather than simply ordinary chocolate milk.	chocolate drink	He grabbed a cold Yoo-hoo from the fridge.	Brand-reference card. Avoid locking the definition to a specific formulation because ingredients/products can change.		
