186	1855	1958	betray / betrays	/bɪˈtreɪz/	verb	To be disloyal to or violate someone's trust; to reveal or disclose something, including unintentionally through signs or behavior.	deceive, sell out; reveal, give away	He betrayed his friend. / Her voice betrayed her nervousness.	KEY POLYSEMY: betray a person/trust/secret = disloyalty or disclosure; 'his expression betrayed his fear' = unintentionally revealed it. Normalize base + source form.		
