187	1868	1971	tonsil / tonsils	/ˈtɑnsəl/	noun (anatomy)	A mass of lymphoid tissue in the throat region; in everyday usage 'the tonsils' usually means the paired palatine tonsils visible at the back of the throat.	lymphoid tissue; palatine tonsil (specific)	His tonsils were swollen. / She had her tonsils removed as a child.	PRECISION: there are multiple tonsillar tissues (palatine, pharyngeal/adenoid, lingual, etc.); the common pair are palatine tonsils. Not accurately a generic 'throat gland'.		
