193	1923	2028	lanyard	/ˈlænjɚd/	noun	A cord, strap, or line used to secure, carry, suspend, or attach something, commonly worn around the neck/wrist for an ID, keys, whistle, etc.; also has nautical/technical uses.	strap, cord, neck strap	Wear your badge on the lanyard. / She clipped her keys to a wrist lanyard.	Broaden beyond neck/wrist: the core is a securing/attachment cord or strap. 'Badge holder' may be attached to a lanyard but is not the same object.		
