198	1972	2078	erasure	/ɪˈreɪʒɚ/	noun	The act/process or result of erasing, deleting, removing, effacing, or making something absent/invisible; figuratively used of history, identity, culture, contribution, memory, etc.	deletion, removal, effacement, obliteration	The essay discusses the erasure of women's contributions from the historical record.	Broader than identity politics. Word family: erase. In social/cultural discussion, 'erasure of X' often means omission or rendering X invisible, not literal deletion.		
