198	1978	2084	conflict-free diamond	/nɑn ˈkɑnflɪkt ˈdaɪəmənd/ — /ˈkɑnflɪkt friː ˈdaɪəmənd/	noun phrase / ethical-sourcing label	A diamond represented as not financing armed conflict under a specified sourcing/certification framework. The label does not by itself guarantee that every labor, environmental, or broader human-rights concern is absent.	non-conflict diamond (less common), responsibly sourced diamond (broader/different)	She asked whether the jeweler could document that the diamond was conflict-free.	CORRECTION/PRECISION: 'conflict-free' primarily concerns conflict financing; do not automatically equate it with fully ethical labor practices. 'Ethically sourced' is broader and not a synonym.		
