204	2039	2155	auger	/ˈɔɡɚ/	noun; verb	A spiral/helical boring tool used to drill holes or move material, especially in wood, soil, ice, grain, or plumbing; verb: to bore/drill with an auger.	borer, drill (broader)	We used an ice auger to drill a fishing hole. / The crew augered holes for the posts.	Broaden noun + verb. A gimlet is a smaller hand boring tool, not a general synonym.		
