206	2054	2171	brigade	/brɪˈɡeɪd/	noun; verb (internet slang extension)	A military formation consisting of multiple battalions/regiments depending system; also an organized group for a task (fire brigade). Online, 'brigade' can mean coordinate a group to flood/interfere with another community.	military unit, organized group; coordinate mass participation	The fire brigade arrived quickly. / The post was accused of sending users to brigade another forum.	Major modern internet sense useful alongside military/civic sense. Exact military organization varies by armed force.		
