225	2244	2369	impudent / impudence	/ˈɪmpjəd(ə)nt/	adjective; noun	Impudent = boldly disrespectful, rude, or shamelessly forward; impudence = that behavior/quality.	insolent, impertinent, cheeky; disrespect	The impudent reply shocked the teacher. / He had the impudence to demand an apology.	CORRECTION: current POS says adjective/noun form while headword only adjective. Teach family cleanly. Tone stronger/more formal than playful 'cheeky'.		
225	2245	2370	pop a balloon / popping a balloon	/ˈpɑpɪŋ ə bəˈluːn/	literal phrase; source-dependent metaphor	Literally, to burst a balloon. Figuratively, a speaker may creatively compare puncturing optimism, tension, fantasy, or a social setup to popping/deflating a balloon, but there is no single fixed idiomatic meaning. Also appears literally in dating-show formats involving balloons.	burst a balloon; deflate hopes (creative context)	He popped the balloon with a pin. / Her blunt answer felt like popping the bubble of everyone's optimism.	CORRECTION: do not teach a broad list of fixed figurative meanings. Distinguish literal action, creative metaphor, and source-specific dating-show usage.		
