227	2261	2387	devolve / devolve into; devolve to	/dɪˈvɑlvz/	verb	To deteriorate or descend into a worse/less organized state ('devolve into'); separately, to transfer power, responsibility, or duties to a lower/local level ('devolve to/on').	degenerate, deteriorate; delegate, transfer	The debate devolved into shouting. / Some powers were devolved to regional governments.	CORRECTION: current card misses the major governance/transfer sense. KEY FRAMES: devolve into chaos; devolve power/responsibility to a lower level.		
227	2262	2388	delegate	/ˈdɛlɪˌɡeɪt/	verb; noun	Verb /ˈdɛləˌɡeɪt/: to entrust a task, responsibility, or authority to another person. Noun /ˈdɛləɡət/: a representative sent to a meeting/conference.	assign, entrust; representative	A good manager delegates routine tasks. / Each branch sent a delegate to the convention.	IMPORTANT pronunciation/POS distinction: verb stress differs from noun. KEY FRAME: delegate X to Y.		
