253	2525	2664	ode; OD / odee (NYC slang spelling varies)	/oʊd/ (slang: 'oh-dee')	noun; slang intensifier (distinct items)	Ode = a lyric poem or expressive work of praise/tribute. Separately, NYC/AAVE-influenced slang 'OD' (often pronounced 'oh-dee' and variably spelled online) can mean excessively, extremely, or a lot.	tribute poem; extremely, excessively (slang OD)	The song is an ode to her hometown. / Slang: That line was OD long. / You're doing OD right now.	CORRECTION: the slang intensifier is historically/orthographically 'OD' (from overdose), not the ordinary word 'ode', even if eye-dialect spellings such as 'odee' appear. Keep the two lexical items separate.		
253	2526	2665	autocratically	/ˌɔtəˈkrætɪkli/	adverb	In a way that concentrates decision-making or authority in one ruler/leader and allows little meaningful participation or constraint.	authoritatively, dictatorially (stronger), unilaterally	He ran the organization autocratically, making major decisions without consultation.	Do not make 'oppressively' a necessary synonym; autocratic describes power/decision structure, though it can coexist with oppression.		
253	2527	2666	autocracy	/ɔˈtɑkrəsi/	noun	A system of government in which supreme political power is concentrated in one ruler or a very small ruling center with limited effective constraints; by extension, highly centralized one-person rule.	one-person rule, authoritarian rule (broader), dictatorship (overlapping)	The coup replaced the fragile democracy with an autocracy.	PRECISION: dictatorship, authoritarianism, and autocracy overlap but are not perfect synonyms in political science.		
