256	2552	2692	bathroom vanity; be in the toilet	/ˈvænəti ɪn ˈtɔɪlət/	two separate expressions	A bathroom vanity is a sink/counter/cabinet unit. Separately, informal 'X is in the toilet' means X (e.g. reputation, morale, economy) is in a very bad state. 'Vanity in toilet' is not a standard combined expression.	vanity unit; be in terrible shape, be down the drain (contextual)	We replaced the bathroom vanity. / After the scandal, his reputation was in the toilet.	CORRECTION: split two unrelated constructions. A vanity is not normally 'in the toilet'; and 'vanity was in the toilet' is only a creative/contextual metaphor, not a lexicalized sense.		
