257	2565	2705	no torpedo in the tube	/noʊ tɔrˈpidoʊ ɪn ðə tub/	source-specific comedic euphemism	A deliberately absurd euphemistic image for difficulty defecating/constipation in the source context; not a standard English idiom.	constipation joke, can't poop (informal)	He jokingly described the problem as 'no torpedo in the tube.'	Keep as source/cultural recognition, not productive standard slang. Meaning depends on the source joke.		
