258	2574	2714	put out / put oneself out / put out (sexual slang)	/pʊt aʊt/	phrasal verb constructions	Put out = extinguish; produce/issue; inconvenience or trouble ('be put out'); put oneself out = make special effort; vulgar/dated sexual slang 'put out' = agree to have sex.	extinguish, issue, inconvenience; make an effort; have sex (slang)	Put the fire out. / The studio put out a new trailer. / She really put herself out to help. / The sexual sense can sound objectifying.	Major polysemy. CORRECTION: distinguish 'put oneself out' from bare 'put out'; sexual sense is often judgmental/objectifying and recognition-focused.		
