259	2585	2726	channel / channeling	/ˈʧænəlɪŋ/	verb	To direct something through a particular route; figuratively, to direct emotion/energy into an activity or act as a medium for purported spiritual communication.	direct, funnel, harness; mediate	She channeled her frustration into exercise. / The medium claimed to be channeling a spirit.	Normalize base + source form. Separate ordinary figurative 'channel energy/emotion into X' from spiritualist sense.		
