262	2618	2761	the medium is the message	/ˈmiːdiəm ɪz ðə ˈmɛsɪdʒ/	media-theory phrase / quotation	Marshall McLuhan's formulation that the characteristics and social effects of a communication medium itself shape human experience and society, not merely the content it carries.	McLuhan's media theory, medium shapes experience	For McLuhan, 'the medium is the message' directs attention to how a medium restructures patterns of perception and social life.	CORRECTION: avoid reducing the idea to 'form influences perception more than content'. The claim is broader: the medium's form/effects are themselves a consequential 'message'.		
