266	2656	2799	ease / ease off	/iz/	noun; verb; phrasal verb	Ease noun = absence of difficulty/discomfort or relaxed manner. Verb = reduce pain/difficulty/tension or move gently. Ease off = lessen in intensity or reduce pressure/effort.	comfort, facility; relieve, lessen; let up	She answered with ease. / The medicine eased the pain. / The rain eased off by evening.	Broaden major noun/verb senses. Common: at ease, with ease, ease into, ease up/off.		
