270	2692	2837	stall someone / stall for time; stall out	/stɔl mi aʊt/	verb constructions	To deliberately delay someone or delay action by evasion, excuses, or tactics; 'stall for time' = intentionally create delay. Separately, 'stall out' means stop functioning/progressing and is not normally a transitive 'stall me out' idiom.	delay, hold up, stonewall; buy time	I think he's stalling me until the deadline passes. / She stalled for time while the team checked the figures.	CORRECTION: normalize nonstandard 'stall me out'. Remove corrupted unrelated Japanese/otaku comparison. Teach stall + person and stall for time vs intransitive stall out.		
