285	2842	2993	no fruit left unturned	/noʊ frut lɛft ʌnˈtɜrnd/	playful idiom (nonstandard)	A playful, nonstandard twist on 'leave no stone unturned', substituting fruit for comic/contextual effect while retaining the idea of searching or trying thoroughly.	exhaustive effort, thorough search	We sampled every stall at the market—no fruit left unturned.	KEEP creative source expression. CORRECTION/CLEANUP: remove mojibake. Standard idiom is 'leave no stone unturned' = make every possible effort / search thoroughly. Use fruit version only as deliberate wordplay.		
