285	2847	2999	take up	/teɪk ʌp/	phrasal verb	Highly polysemous phrasal verb: begin a hobby/activity; occupy time/space; accept an offer/challenge ('take someone up on X'); raise/discuss an issue; resume/continue from a point; shorten clothing, among other senses.	start, begin, accept, occupy, engage in	She took up painting. / The sofa takes up too much space. / I'll take you up on that offer. / Let's take the issue up tomorrow.	DEPTH: distinguish take up + activity/space/topic from take PERSON up on + offer/challenge. This card overlaps earlier take-up cards but is useful as a polysemy hub.		
