286	2854	3007	by contrast / in contrast	/baɪ ˈkɑn.træst/ | /ɪn ˈkɑn.træst/	contrast markers	Both mark a difference. 'In contrast' commonly appears in 'in contrast to/with X'; 'by contrast' is especially natural as a sentence-level connector comparing with what was just mentioned.	conversely, on the other hand	In contrast to last week, today is cold. / Her brother loves crowds. By contrast, she prefers quiet places.	Duplicate-topic card retained as a usage comparison. Do not teach the distinction as merely formal vs informal or purely positional.		
