287	2866	3019	decimal vs. integer	/ˈdɛs.ə.məl/ vs /ˈɪn.tɪ.dʒɚ/	math comparison	An integer is a whole number (...−2, −1, 0, 1, 2...) with no fractional part. A decimal is a base-10 notation/representation using a decimal point; decimals can represent integers too (e.g., 5.0).	integer, decimal notation, non-integer decimal	5 is an integer; 5.75 is not. / 5.0 is a decimal representation of the integer 5.	CORRECTION: 'decimal' is not simply the opposite of integer. A decimal representation may denote an integer; 'non-integer' is the precise contrast when fractional value matters.		
