288	2875	3030	bear testimony to / bear witness to	/bɛrz ˈtɛs.təˌmoʊ.ni/	formal verb constructions	To serve as evidence of or attest to something. 'Bear witness to' is much more common in modern English; 'bear testimony to' is formal and less frequent.	attest to, testify to, demonstrate, bear witness to	The surviving letters bear witness to their friendship. / The ruins bear testimony to the city's long history.	Normalize construction: bear testimony to + X. Do not use bare 'bears testimony' without the complement when teaching the pattern.		
