294	2935	3091	one's loins burn / a fire in one's loins	/bɜrnd ɪn lɔɪnz/	literary/creative sexual imagery	A literary, archaic-sounding, or deliberately comic way to describe strong sexual desire using 'loins' (the lower torso/genital region in older/euphemistic language) and burning imagery.	burn with desire, feel lust, be sexually aroused	The parody described him as having 'a fire in his loins.'	CORRECTION: 'burned in loins' is not a standard idiom. Treat as creative/literary imagery; normal modern English would say 'burn with desire' or simply 'be turned on' depending register.		
