300	2996	3159	desecration	/ˌdɛsəˈkreɪʃən/	noun	The act of violating, damaging, or treating with serious disrespect something regarded as sacred, holy, or deeply revered.	defilement, sacrilege, profanation	Vandalizing the shrine was condemned as desecration.	'Violent' is not required; disrespectful use, damage, or profanation can constitute desecration.		
