301	3003	3166	squeeze in / squeeze something in	/skwiːz ɪn/	phrasal verb	To manage to fit an activity/person into limited time, or fit something into limited physical space.	fit in, make time for, cram in	I squeezed in a workout before work. / Can we squeeze one more chair in?	KEY FRAMES: squeeze X in; squeeze in X; squeeze PERSON in for an appointment. Covers both time and physical space.		
301	3004	3167	garbled characters / mojibake	/ˈɡɑrbəld ˈkærɪktɚz/	noun phrase; technical term	Unreadable, incorrect, or scrambled-looking text characters, often caused by an encoding/decoding mismatch. 'Mojibake' is the specific computing term for garbled text produced by character-encoding problems.	corrupted text, mojibake (encoding-specific), scrambled characters	The file opened with garbled characters because it was decoded with the wrong character encoding.	PRECISION: not all garbled characters are caused by encoding, but mojibake specifically is. Useful given earlier café/détente corruption in this Master.		
