302	3012	3178	onward / onwards	/ˈɑnwɚd/	adverb; adjective	Forward in space or progress; from a specified time/point and continuing after it.	forward, ahead; from then on	From 2025 onward, the rule applies to all new accounts. / They pressed onward despite the rain.	AmE commonly 'onward'; BrE also 'onwards' as adverb. Useful frame: from X onward(s).		
