302	3014	3180	apron belly / abdominal pannus (source: 'flap belly')	/flæp ˈbɛli/	informal term; medical/anatomical term	'Apron belly' is an informal term for an overhanging fold of abdominal skin and/or fatty tissue. 'Pannus' or 'abdominal pannus' is a clinical/anatomical term used in some contexts. 'Flap belly' is not a standard general term.	apron belly, abdominal pannus, panniculus (technical/contextual)	After major weight loss, some people are left with an overhanging fold of abdominal skin.	CORRECTION: normalize away from nonstandard 'flap belly'. Avoid implying surgery is required; management depends on symptoms, goals, and clinical context.		
