302	3020	3186	tease	/tiːz/	verb; noun	Verb: make playful jokes at someone's expense, provoke playfully, tempt without satisfying, or reveal a small preview. Noun: a person who teases, or a preview/teaser-like act in some contexts; 'a tease' can also carry flirtatious/sexual implications.	joke with, rib, taunt (harsher), tempt, preview	I'm just teasing you. / The trailer teased the villain without showing him. / He's such a tease.	Broaden major senses. 'Taunt' is usually more hostile. Sexual/flirtatious noun use can be judgmental depending context.		
