306	3059	3229	cognate	/ˈkɑɡneɪt/	noun; adjective (linguistics)	A word related to another through descent from the same ancestral word; adjective: related by common linguistic origin. More broadly/formally, 'cognate' can mean related or akin.	related word, etymological relative, akin (broader adjective)	English 'mother' and German 'Mutter' are cognates. / English 'father' and Spanish 'padre' are cognate forms.	CORRECTION: cognates are not merely words that look/sound alike, and they need not have identical meanings. Replace incorrect Spanish/French 'comer' example. Distinguish false friends and loanwords.		
