308	3073	3243	emanate / emanate from	/ˈɛməˌneɪt/	verb	To come or flow out from a source, especially light, sound, smell, heat, influence, or an impression/quality.	radiate, issue, come from, flow from	A strange smell emanated from the basement. / Warmth seemed to emanate from her voice.	KEY FRAME: X emanates from SOURCE. For qualities, 'PERSON emanates confidence' occurs, but 'confidence emanates from PERSON' or 'PERSON exudes confidence' is often more natural.		
