309	3083	3255	my circuits must be crossed / one's wires are crossed	/maɪ ˈsɝkɪts məst bi krɔst/	creative humorous expression; related idiom	'My circuits must be crossed' is a humorous technology/brain metaphor for being confused or mentally mixed up. The established idiom 'get/have one's wires crossed' means misunderstand one another or mix up information.	my wires are crossed, I'm mixed up, I'm confused	I wrote down Tuesday instead of Thursday—my circuits must be crossed. / We got our wires crossed about the meeting time.	SOURCE/CREATIVE CAUTION: 'circuits must be crossed' is understandable wordplay, but 'get/have one's wires crossed' is the conventional idiom. Clean corrupted apostrophe.		
