310	3091	3268	stroke	/stroʊk/	noun; verb	Highly polysemous. Noun: a single movement/blow/mark; a swimming movement/style; a clock strike; a medical stroke (acute brain injury from interrupted blood flow or bleeding). Verb: move a hand gently over something; make a stroke; in rowing, set the pace as stroke/stroke seat.	movement, blow, mark; caress (verb)	She painted with broad strokes. / He had a stroke and was taken to the hospital. / She stroked the cat's fur. / His golf stroke has improved.	MEDICAL PRECISION: a stroke is not simply 'loss of brain function'; it is an acute neurological event caused by disrupted cerebral blood flow or bleeding. Keep other senses clearly separate.		
