310	3094	3271	comminuted	/ˈkɒməˌnjuːtɪd/	adjective; past participle (technical)	Broken, crushed, or divided into multiple small fragments; medically, a comminuted fracture is a bone fracture in which the bone is broken into more than two pieces/fragments.	fragmented, crushed, pulverized; multifragmentary (medical/contextual)	The X-ray showed a comminuted fracture of the femur. / The material is comminuted before further processing.	Technical. Remove speculative metaphorical use unless sourced; common in medicine and particle-size/material processing.		
