319	3189	3374	employee reassignment	/ɛmˈplɔɪi riəˈsaɪnmənt/	noun phrase	The process of moving an employee to a different role, team, or location within an organization.	transfer, role change, repositioning	Her employee reassignment came after the department restructure.	Core meaning retained. Depth QA: strengthen natural collocations, grammatical frame, register, and reusable literal/figurative patterns where useful.		
