355	3542	3788	undercut	/ˌʌndərˈkʌt/	verb, noun	Verb: to weaken or undermine; to sell at a lower price. Noun: a cut made underneath something.	undermine, underprice	Cheap imports undercut domestic manufacturers.	Figurative and literal meanings; also hairstyle term. 日本語では「切り下げる」「弱体化させる」。		
