355	3546	3792	delve into vs dive into		verb phrases	Delve into: to investigate, research, or explore something deeply and methodically. Dive into: to begin something eagerly, energetically, or without hesitation.	explore vs plunge into	She delved into the archives for her research, while he dove into his new project with enthusiasm.	Nuance: 'delve' = methodical depth; 'dive' = energetic entry. Delve emphasizes depth, detail, and thoroughness; often about study, research, or analysis. e.g., “delve into history” (歴史を掘り下げる). Dive emphasizes speed, enthusiasm, and immersion; often about starting an activity. e.g., “dive into work” (仕事に飛び込む). 日本語では「delve into＝掘り下げる」「dive into＝勢いよく取り組む」。		
