355	3549	3796	slant / slanted / at a slant		noun; adjective; phrase	A slant is a slope or angle away from horizontal/vertical; figuratively, it is a particular biased angle or point of view. 'Slanted' can mean physically angled or biased.	angle, slope; bias, spin; tilted, skewed	The roof rises at a steep slant. / The article gives a slanted account of the dispute.	NORMALIZATION: 'slanting manner' is not a useful fixed phrase. For physical posture say 'at an angle/on a slant'; for biased presentation use 'slanted' or 'a slant on X'.		
