356	3551	3798	at the same time: simultaneously / concurrently / at once		adverb contrast	'Simultaneously' means at exactly or effectively the same time. 'Concurrently' means during overlapping periods or in parallel, not necessarily beginning/ending at the same instant. 'At once' can mean simultaneously, but also immediately.	simultaneously, concurrently, at once, together	Both alarms went off simultaneously. / She was working on two projects concurrently. / He tried to answer both questions at once.	NORMALIZATION: replace question-form headword with a reusable contrast card.		
