356	3555	3802	broad-minded	/ˌbrɔːdˈmaɪndɪd/	adjective	Willing to accept different opinions, beliefs, or behaviors without prejudice.	open-minded, tolerant, liberal	She is broad-minded about different cultural practices.	Opposite: narrow-minded. 日本語では「心が広い」「寛容な」。		
356	3556	3803	scoop up	/skuːp ʌp/	phrasal verb	To lift or pick up something quickly, often in one motion.	pick up, gather	He scooped up the toys before guests arrived.	Can also mean acquiring quickly (e.g., 'scoop up a bargain'). 日本語では「すくい上げる」「素早く集める」。		
356	3557	3804	for good	/ˈrʌnɪŋ fər ɡʊd/	adverbial phrase	Permanently; forever, with no intention or expectation of returning to the previous state.	permanently, forever, once and for all	She left the city for good. / Is the restaurant closed for good?	FIX: 'running for good' is not a general fixed phrase. The reusable expression is 'for good', which attaches to many verbs: leave, quit, close, move away, disappear, etc.		
