358	3573	3822	ringleader	/ˈrɪŋˌliːdər/	noun	A person who leads others, especially in unlawful or mischievous activities.	leader, instigator, mastermind	The police arrested the ringleader of the gang.	'Ring' here refers to a physical or figurative circle formed by onlookers or participants, such as in a circus or public spectacle, where the leader directs the action. The term evolved to mean the main instigator of wrongdoing. Unlike 'leader', which can be neutral or positive, 'ringleader' often implies leading harmful, mischievous, or illicit activities. 日本語では「首謀者」「黒幕」「悪事のリーダー」。		
