358	3576	3825	rebut / rebuttal	/rɪˈbʌtɪd/	verb; noun	To respond to an argument, claim, accusation, or evidence by presenting reasons or evidence intended to show that it is false, weak, or unconvincing.	refute, counter, answer, contest	The lawyer rebutted the claim with new evidence. / Her rebuttal addressed each point in turn.	NORMALIZATION: use base form 'rebut'. Rebut does not guarantee that the other side has been conclusively 'defeated' or left unable to respond; it means present a counterargument or contrary evidence.		
358	3577	4632	Maslow's hierarchy of needs	/ˈmæz.loʊz ˈhaɪ.rɑːr.ki əv niːdz/	proper noun / psychology concept	A model associated with psychologist Abraham Maslow that organizes human needs from basic physiological and safety needs toward belonging, esteem, and self-actualization.	hierarchy of needs, Maslow's model	The textbook used Maslow's hierarchy of needs to discuss motivation.	Often shown as a pyramid, although Maslow himself did not originally present the theory in the familiar pyramid form.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0101 | searches: maslow
