358	3580	4501	in the sidebar	/ɪn ðə ˈsaɪd.bɑːr/	UI / publishing phrase	Located in a secondary panel or column beside the main content of a page, document, or interface.	in the side panel, in the side column	You'll find the filters in the sidebar on the left.	Sidebar is normally one word. In legal contexts, sidebar can also mean a private discussion at the judge's bench.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0108 | searches: in side bar meaning
359	3581	4060	comic strip	/ˈkɑː.mɪk strɪp/	noun	A short sequence of illustrated panels, usually with dialogue or captions, that tells a joke or brief story.	cartoon strip	The newspaper runs a comic strip on the back page every day.	Often serialized around recurring characters. Distinct from a single-panel cartoon and from a full comic book.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0107 | searches: comic strip example
359	3582	5276	wrangle	/ˈræŋ.ɡəl/	verb; noun	To argue or negotiate in a difficult, prolonged way; also to manage, gather, or control people, animals, data, or other unruly things.	argue, negotiate, manage, corral	We spent an hour wrangling over the contract. / She had to wrangle data from five different systems.	Common patterns: wrangle over/about something; wrangle with someone; wrangle something into shape. 'Data wrangling' is common in computing/data work. Historically also associated with handling livestock.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0103, voca_0106 | searches: define wrangle | wrangle
