361	3604	4147	differential	/ˌdɪf.əˈren.ʃəl/	noun / adjective	A difference or gap between amounts, rates, groups, or conditions; also relating to differences between things.	difference, gap, disparity	The pay differential between the two roles has narrowed.	Common in economics, medicine, engineering, math, and mechanics: wage differential, differential diagnosis, differential equation, car differential.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0108 | searches: differential
361	3605	5233	ward	/wɔːrd/	noun; verb	A distinct section of a hospital; a person under another's legal protection or guardianship; or an administrative district. As a verb, usually in ward off, it means repel or prevent.	hospital unit, district, dependent	She was moved from the emergency department to the cardiac ward.	Several unrelated common senses. In fantasy, ward can also mean a protective spell/barrier. Do not confuse the noun with the phrasal verb ward off.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0106 | searches: ward meaning
