Not me staring at my phone instead of answering the call.
Not me thinking I could finish all of this in one night."	The literal grammar points away from the speaker ('not me'), but the meme meaning points straight back at them: 'Yes, this is absolutely me, and I know how ridiculous/embarrassing/relatable it is.' The humor comes from mock denial immediately undercut by the -ing phrase. Japanese does not have a single fixed equivalent, but the feel can be close to ironic self-denial such as 「いやいや、まさか私が一袋全部食べてるとか……」「私が電話無視して画面見つめてるわけないじゃん（笑）」—where the context makes it obvious that the speaker is in fact doing exactly that. Often conveys playful embarrassment, self-mockery, disbelief at oneself, or 'caught myself doing it again' energy.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0100 | searches: not me thinking meme
