378	3777	5358	innocent (naive / inexperienced sense)	/ˈɪn.ə.sənt/	adjective	Naive, inexperienced, unsophisticated, or unworldly, sometimes in an appealingly childlike way; not only the legal/moral sense 'not guilty.'	naive, inexperienced, unworldly, childlike	He had an innocent view of how the industry worked and assumed everyone would play fair.	Useful for some contexts of Japanese おぼこい. 'Innocent' can sound warm or sympathetic; 'naive' more readily suggests poor judgment due to inexperience; 'childlike' is often positive, while 'childish' is usually critical. Retain this sense-specific card even though #5050 is a broader Japanese→English choice map.		voca_0099–0109 | reviewed improved card
