The company absorbed the extra cost."	Useful senses: absorb liquid/energy; absorb information; absorb a shock/impact; absorb a cost/loss.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0106 | searches: absorb
390	3894	3936	a big fish in a small pond	/ə ˌbɪɡ fɪʃ ɪn ə ˌsmɔːl ˈpɑːnd/	idiom	An important or influential person in a small or limited setting, whose status might be less impressive in a larger arena.	important person in a small circle	He was a big fish in a small pond at his local firm.	Contrast with being a small fish in a big pond.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0108 | searches: big fish small pond meaning
390	3895	3856	aggro	/ˈæɡ.roʊ/	noun, adjective (informal); verb (gaming)	Aggressive behavior, conflict, or hassle; in gaming, the hostility or attention an enemy directs toward a player.	aggression, hassle, hostility	"I don’t want any aggro tonight.
