391	3910	4230	engrossed	/ɪnˈɡroʊst/	adjective	So absorbed in something that you give it all your attention.	absorbed, immersed, captivated	She was so engrossed in the book that she missed her stop.	Common pattern: engrossed in something.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0102, voca_0103 | searches: define engrossed | engrossed meaning
392	3911	4339	geek out	/ɡiːk ˈaʊt/	phrasal verb, informal	To become very enthusiastic and talk or think intensely about a subject one loves, especially a specialized interest.	geek out over/about, nerd out, enthuse, get really into	We spent an hour geeking out over old cameras. / I geeked out when I saw the original animation cels. / They immediately started geeking out about the sound design.	Usually positive/playful and self-aware rather than insulting. Common patterns: geek out over/about X. It suggests enthusiastic absorption in niche, technical, fandom, or specialist details.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0107 | searches: geek out
