392	3913	5403	extenuating circumstances	/ɪkˈsten.ju.eɪ.t̬ɪŋ ˈsɝː.kəm.stæn.sɪz/	plural noun phrase	Circumstances that make an offense, mistake, or failure seem less serious or more understandable, potentially reducing blame or punishment.	mitigating circumstances	The judge considered the extenuating circumstances before sentencing.	Close to 'mitigating circumstances.' 'Extenuating' emphasizes making the wrongdoing appear less serious; 'mitigating' more broadly reduces severity, blame, or punishment.		voca_0099–0109 | reviewed improved card
