392	3916	5439	commiserate with someone	/kəˈmɪz.ə.reɪt/	verb phrase	To express or share sympathy with someone about a disappointment, difficulty, or misfortune.	sympathize with	We commiserated with each other over the canceled trip.	Patterns: commiserate with someone; commiserate over/about something. Often implies shared 'that sucks' sympathy rather than solemn condolence.		voca_0099–0109 | reviewed improved card
392	3917	4146	humanity	/hjuːˈmæn.ə.t̬i/	noun	Human beings collectively; the state or condition of being human; or the quality of being humane, compassionate, and kind toward others.	humankind, mankind; compassion, humaneness	"The disaster brought out the best in humanity.
