395	3944	4300	flop vs. hit	/flɑːp vɝː.səs hɪt/	contrast card	A flop is a work, product, or event that fails badly, especially commercially or popularly; a hit is one that achieves strong success or popularity.	failure vs. success, bomb vs. smash hit	The first film was a flop, but its sequel became a surprise hit.	Especially common for movies, shows, songs, products, and performances. A bomb can mean a flop in U.S. English.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0104 | searches: flop vs hit
395	3945	5464	temperament	/ˈtem.pɚ.ə.mənt/	noun	A person's characteristic emotional nature and habitual way of reacting to people, situations, and stimulation.	disposition, nature, character, personality	"The twins differ greatly in temperament.
