395	3946	4046	circuitous	/sɚˈkjuː.ə.təs/	adjective	Longer and less direct than necessary, either physically or in speech, reasoning, or explanation.	roundabout, indirect	We took a circuitous route through the mountains.	Can describe routes, explanations, arguments, and methods.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0107 | searches: circuitous
395	3947	5437	externalize	/ɪkˈstɝː.nəl.aɪz/	verb	To express or project something internal outwardly; or to shift costs, responsibility, or problems onto an outside party.	project, express outwardly; shift	Some people externalize stress as anger. / The company externalized part of the environmental cost.	Useful two-domain word: psychology = make inner states outward; economics/business = push costs or burdens outside the decision-maker. Contrast internalize.		voca_0099–0109 | reviewed improved card
