395	3949	4195	down the hatch	/daʊn ðə hætʃ/	idiom	Said when swallowing food, drink, or medicine, especially quickly or in one go.	here goes, bottoms up	Down the hatch—this medicine tastes awful.	Can accompany drinking or swallowing; it is not simply a synonym for 'down a drink.'		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0107 | searches: down the hatch meaning
