397	3961	5498	side couple	/ˈsaɪd ˌkʌpəl/	noun; square-dance term / niche internet relationship slang	1. In square dancing, one of the couples positioned at the sides of the square, as opposed to the head couples. 2. In niche online relationship usage, a secondary or hidden pairing/relationship alongside primary partners; this sense is context-dependent and not general everyday usage.	side pair (square dance, descriptive); secondary couple, side relationship (niche relationship sense)	The side couples waited while the head couples began the figure. / In that online discussion, the two were described as a side couple even though both already had primary partners.	KEEP + EXPAND. The square-dance sense is established. The relationship sense is niche/nonstandard internet usage and should not be assumed without context.		Supplemental from approved batch 4712–4761
