401	4006	5108	it / that / something will be a hoot	/ɪt wɪl bi ə huːt/	conversational pattern, informal	Used to predict that an event, activity, situation, or experience will be very funny, entertaining, or enjoyable.	it'll be great fun, it'll be a riot	You should come to karaoke with us—that'll be a hoot.	Keep this contextual pattern even though the base noun hoot already exists: the predictive frame 'That'll be a hoot' is highly reusable and may be easier to acquire as a chunk. Hoot itself can mean a funny/enjoyable person, thing, or experience. Variants: It'll be a hoot; That should be a hoot; The trip was a hoot.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0107 | searches: that will be a hoot meaning
401	4007	3948	blunt	/blʌnt/	adjective / verb	Direct and unsoftened in speech; not sharp; as a verb, to make something less sharp, intense, or effective.	direct, frank; dull	"I'll be blunt: the plan isn't working.
