401	4009	5497	nobody	/ˈnoʊˌbɑː.di/	noun, informal	A person with little or no social importance, recognition, influence, or status.	unknown, nonentity	I was basically a nobody in high school.	Especially useful for status/visibility: being a nobody means people do not know or regard you as important; it does not necessarily mean actively disliked or excluded.		Supplemental from approved batch 4662–4711
401	4010	4834	purge	/pɝːdʒ/	verb; noun	To remove people or things considered unwanted, harmful, or impure, often thoroughly or forcefully.	eliminate, clear out, expel	The company purged outdated records from the system.	Can refer to political expulsions, data cleanup, bodily clearing, or removing unwanted material.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0104 | searches: purge meaning
402	4011	5128	tickled pink		idiom, informal	Extremely pleased, delighted, or amused.	delighted, thrilled, overjoyed, pleased as punch	She was tickled pink by the surprise party.	Playful and somewhat old-fashioned but still recognizable.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0100, voca_0101 | searches: tickled pink meaning
402	4012	5000	snow someone	/snoʊ/	verb, informal, chiefly North American	To deceive, overwhelm, or persuade someone with impressive-sounding talk, charm, or a flood of information.	deceive, bamboozle, overwhelm with talk	Don't let the salesman snow you with technical jargon.	Yes: snow can mean trick/deceive, often by burying someone in persuasive talk or information.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0101 | searches: snow verb means to trick?
402	4013	5272	Worcestershire	UK /ˈwʊs.tə.ʃə(r)/; US /ˈwʊs.tɚ.ʃɚ/	proper noun	A county in west-central England; also familiar to many learners from the name Worcestershire sauce.	Worcester county (contextual)	She grew up in Worcestershire, not far from the Malvern Hills.	The spelling is famously misleading to learners: the middle letters are heavily reduced in pronunciation. Do not confuse the county name with 'Worcestershire sauce,' though the sauce takes its name from Worcester/Worcestershire.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0107 | searches: Worcestershire definition | Cambridge English Dictionary
402	4014	4023	celibate	/ˈsel.ə.bət/	adjective / noun	Not engaging in sexual activity, often as a personal, religious, or vocational choice; a person who lives that way.	abstinent	He chose to remain celibate for religious reasons.	Celibate often suggests a deliberate or sustained state. Compare abstinent, which can be broader and temporary.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0100 | searches: define celibate
402	4015	4995	SMDH	/ˌes.em.diːˈeɪtʃ/	internet/text abbreviation	An emphatic variant of SMH, commonly expanded as 'shaking my damn head,' expressing disbelief, frustration, disappointment, or disapproval.	SMH, unbelievable	SMDH, I can't believe they did that again.	Very informal texting/social-media abbreviation. The D intensifies SMH; expansions may vary in wording.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0107 | searches: smdh meaning
