403	4022	4859	read away	/riːd əˈweɪ/	verb phrase	To continue reading freely or for some time; in an imperative, 'read away' can mean go ahead and read without hesitation.	keep reading, read on	If you're curious, read away—I've got plenty of books.	Not a strongly fixed phrasal verb. Away adds continuation or permission, as in work away, chat away.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0108 | searches: read away meaning
