403	4027	4314	fort vs. fortress	/fɔːrt vɝː.səs ˈfɔːr.trəs/	contrast card	A fort is a fortified military post or defensive structure; a fortress is a large, heavily fortified stronghold designed to resist attack.	defensive post vs. fortified stronghold	The outpost was a small fort, while the old city was protected by a massive fortress.	Fort is broader and often smaller; fortress strongly suggests size, strength, and formidable defenses.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0108 | searches: fort vs fortress
