428	4280	4157	discrete vs. discreet	/dɪˈskriːt/ vs. /dɪˈskriːt/	contrast pair	Discrete means separate, individually distinct, or consisting of separate units. Discreet means careful, tactful, unobtrusive, or good at keeping private matters confidential.	discrete: separate, distinct; discreet: tactful, prudent, unobtrusive	"The data are divided into three discrete categories.
She was discreet about the confidential conversation."	Same pronunciation, different spelling and meaning. Memory hook: discrete keeps things separate; discreet describes careful/private behavior. Related nouns: discreteness = the quality of being separate/distinct; discreetness = tact, prudence, or unobtrusiveness. Discretion is related to discreet but has broader meanings: freedom/authority to decide using one's own judgment, and careful/tactful handling of sensitive matters.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0107 | searches: discrete vs discreet
