433	4327	5458	something brewing inside someone	/ˈsʌm.θɪŋ ˈbruː.ɪŋ ɪnˈsaɪd ˈsʌm.wʌn/	figurative phrase / pattern	Something—usually a feeling, tension, conflict, or idea—is gradually developing within a person before becoming fully visible or expressed.	building up inside, simmering, developing internally	There was clearly something brewing inside him, but he wasn't ready to talk about it.	Broader reusable pattern related to “brewing in your chest.” Can refer to emotion, tension, resentment, excitement, an idea, or an internal change that is still developing.		User-approved supplemental entry from batch 3712–3761.
