433	4330	5479	queen bee	/ˈkwiːn ˌbiː/	noun, informal	A dominant, influential, or socially central woman or girl in a group, especially one perceived as controlling a clique or social hierarchy.	ringleader, dominant popular girl	She was treated as the queen bee of the school's most exclusive clique.	Often used for a high-status female social leader; can be admiring, teasing, or critical. In school-movie/pop-culture stereotypes, the queen bee is often the leader of the popular clique.		Supplemental from approved batch 4662–4711
