434	4335	5311	a mixed bag (玉石混交)	/ə mɪkst bæɡ/	idiom	A mixture containing things of different kinds or quality, especially a combination of good and bad elements.	mixed assortment, mixture, uneven set	The submissions were a mixed bag: a few were excellent, but many were weak.	A natural English equivalent for 玉石混交 in many everyday contexts. It emphasizes an uneven mixture of good and bad or varied things. For a more literary image, English also has 'the wheat and the chaff,' especially when separating valuable material from worthless material.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0101 | searches: 玉石混交　意味
