434	4340	5261	slightly inflected (tone / voice)	/ˈslaɪt.li ɪnˈflek.tɪd/	adjective phrase	Having a small but noticeable change or modulation in pitch, stress, intonation, or vocal coloring rather than being completely flat or neutral.	slightly modulated, subtly varied	Her tone was slightly inflected, just enough to make the remark sound skeptical.	Here inflected refers to vocal/tone modulation, not grammatical inflection. A slightly inflected tone may carry a subtle emotional or pragmatic cue—skepticism, warmth, irony, hesitation, emphasis—without sounding strongly expressive.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0108 | searches: when tone is slightly inflected, what does that mean?
