436	4351	5322	more than make up for something / more than compensate for something (補って余りある)		idiomatic translation	To compensate for a weakness, loss, or disadvantage so fully that the positive factor not only cancels it out but exceeds what was needed.	more than offset, more than compensate for, more than make up for	The apartment is small, but the incredible view more than makes up for the lack of space.	The key force of 余りある is 'more than enough to compensate.' 'Make up for' is natural and conversational; 'compensate for' is more formal; 'more than offset' works well for costs, disadvantages, or negative effects.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0101 | searches: 補って余りある 英語のフレーズ
