436	4353	4872	reductio ad absurdum	/rɪˌdʌk.ti.oʊ æd əbˈsɝː.dəm/	noun, logic/rhetoric	A method of argument that tests a claim by showing that accepting it leads to an absurd, impossible, or contradictory consequence.	reduction to absurdity	She used reductio ad absurdum to expose the flaw in the rule.	In formal logic it can prove a proposition via contradiction; in ordinary argument it may expose an implication as absurd.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0103 | searches: reductio ad absurdum
436	4354	4714	be onto someone/something	/biː ˈɑːn.tuː/	informal phrase	To have discovered or begun to understand someone's secret, wrongdoing, plan, or the truth about something; also, to have found a promising idea or opportunity.	be wise to, have figured out, be on the trail of	"I think the police are onto him.
