436	4355	4183	dodger	/ˈdɑː.dʒɚ/	noun	A person who avoids something, especially a duty, responsibility, payment, or obligation.	evader, shirker	He was labeled a tax dodger after years of hiding income.	Common compounds: draft dodger, tax dodger. Also the name of a baseball team member in the plural Dodgers.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0108 | searches: dodger meaning
436	4356	5425	waft	/wɑːft/	verb; noun	To move or be carried gently through the air, especially a smell, smoke, music, or another light sensation.	drift, float	The smell of fresh bread wafted through the kitchen.	Often suggests a light, gentle current. 'Drift' is broader and can describe objects, thoughts, water movement, or gradual change; 'waft' strongly evokes air carrying something light.		voca_0099–0109 | reviewed improved card
