437	4366	5256	get backed up	/ɡet bækt ʌp/	phrasal expression	To become delayed, congested, blocked, or accumulated because things cannot move or be processed normally.	get congested, pile up, get delayed	Traffic got backed up for miles after the accident.	Also work/orders can get backed up; drains/toilets can back up; informally a person can be 'backed up' meaning constipated. Context determines the sense.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0106, voca_0107 | searches: what is what does to get backed up means
437	4367	4624	make no bones about something	/meɪk noʊ boʊnz əˈbaʊt ˈsʌm.θɪŋ/	idiom	To state an opinion, intention, or fact openly and directly, without hesitation or attempting to hide it.	be frank about, make no secret of, be unapologetic about	She makes no bones about wanting the top job.	Usually make no bones about + noun/-ing. The expression emphasizes frankness and lack of hesitation.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0108 | searches: make no bones meaning
