438	4379	3840	accusational opposition disorder	/əˌkjuː.zəˈteɪ.ʃən.əl ˌɑː.pəˈzɪʃ.ən dɪsˌɔːr.dɚ/	noun phrase (humorous, coined)	A joking pseudo-diagnosis for habitually disagreeing with people in an accusatory way.	—	She jokingly called his constant finger-pointing “accusational opposition disorder.”	Coined in the TV series Community; not a recognized clinical diagnosis. The humor riffs on psychological/psychiatric diagnostic labels.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0102 | searches: accusational opposition disorder meaning
