439	4382	5243	school belle	/skuːl bel/	noun phrase, old-fashioned	An old-fashioned way to refer to a particularly admired or beautiful young woman at a school; modern English has no single standard title that exactly means 'the most beautiful girl in the school.'	campus beauty, beauty queen (context-dependent)	She was remembered as the school belle, though the phrase sounds old-fashioned today.	Useful cultural-equivalence note: English usually describes the person rather than assigning a fixed title. 'Beauty queen' normally implies a pageant; 'it girl' means fashionable/popular, not simply most beautiful. Search context: https://forum.wordreference.com/threads/most-beautiful-girl.662571/		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0109 | searches: what do you call the most beautiful girl in your school
