454	4536	4056	cold snap	/ˈkoʊld snæp/	noun	A short period of unusually cold weather.	cold spell	A sudden cold snap damaged the early blossoms.	Usually shorter and more sudden than a prolonged cold season.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0108 | searches: cold snap
454	4537	4258	expertly	/ˈek.spɝːt.li/	adverb	In a highly skilled, knowledgeable, or accomplished way.	skillfully, masterfully	She expertly steered the conversation away from the sensitive topic.	Often modifies handled, crafted, performed, navigated, executed.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0101 | searches: expertly
454	4538	4063	commodify	/kəˈmɑː.də.faɪ/	verb	To turn something into a commodity that can be bought, sold, packaged, or commercially exploited.	commercialize, marketize	Critics accused the company of commodifying nostalgia.	Often used critically about culture, identity, attention, art, relationships, or experiences being turned into marketable products.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0105 | searches: commodifying meaning
454	4539	4997	smooth something out	/smuːð ˈsʌm.θɪŋ aʊt/	phrasal verb	To make a surface physically smoother; figuratively, to resolve difficulties, reduce irregularities, or make a process/relationship work more evenly.	even out, resolve, iron out	We need to smooth out a few problems before launch.	Physical and figurative uses are both common.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0107 | searches: smooth out meaning
454	4540	4822	prude	/pruːd/	noun, disapproving	A person who is excessively shocked by or concerned with sexual behavior, nudity, or matters they regard as improper.	puritan, strait-laced person	He called her a prude for objecting to the joke.	Usually judgmental/insulting; it frames the person's standards as excessively restrictive.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0109 | searches: prude meaning
