455	4543	4288	finna	/ˈfɪn.ə/	informal/slang marker	An informal form meaning 'fixing to' or 'about to / going to,' used to express an immediate or intended future action.	about to, going to, fixing to	I'm finna head home.	Associated especially with African American English and Southern U.S. speech; widely used online. Very informal.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0108, voca_0109 | searches: finna meaning
455	4544	4523	interim	/ˈɪn.t̬ɚ.ɪm/	adjective; noun	Temporary and intended to last until a permanent arrangement is made; as a noun, the intervening period.	temporary, provisional, meantime	She was appointed interim director while the board searched for a replacement.	Common: interim report, interim government, interim CEO; in the interim = meanwhile.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0108 | searches: define interim
