458	4580	5294	one's eyes are giving out	/aɪz ɑːr ˈɡɪv.ɪŋ aʊt/	informal expression	One's eyesight or ability to keep using the eyes is beginning to fail or become too strained, tired, or weak to function comfortably.	eyes are failing, eyesight is weakening, eyes are getting tired	I need to stop reading for tonight—my eyes are giving out.	'Give out' means stop functioning or become exhausted. With eyes, it can refer casually to temporary eye strain/fatigue or more seriously to worsening eyesight; context determines how literal or serious it is.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0104 | searches: your eyes are giving out meaning
459	4581	4384	granular	/ˈɡræn.jə.lɚ/	adjective	Consisting of small grains; figuratively, highly detailed or broken down into fine components.	grainy; detailed, fine-grained	The report provides granular data by age, region, and income.	Useful standalone adjective; related to the already-kept phrase get granular about something.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0107 | searches: granular meaning
