466	4657	4616	Machiavellianism	/ˌmæk.i.əˈvel.i.ə.nɪ.zəm/	noun	A tendency or doctrine characterized by strategic manipulation, cynicism, and a willingness to use deception or expedient means to gain or maintain power.	manipulativeness, political cunning, expediency	The character's Machiavellianism makes every alliance feel temporary.	In psychology, Machiavellianism is a personality trait involving manipulativeness and cynical views of others. The popular term is broader than Machiavelli's actual political thought.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0109 | searches: Machiavellianism | machiavellianism
