497	4961	4087	cool off	/ˌkuːl ˈɔːf/	phrasal verb	To become less hot; figuratively, to become calmer or less angry, intense, or enthusiastic.	cool down, calm down	Give him a few minutes to cool off before you talk to him.	Can be physical temperature or emotions. In relationships, cool off can sometimes mean temporarily reduce contact/intensity without necessarily ending the relationship. Contrast: cool off vs break up — cool off can mean temporarily reducing contact/intensity or taking space, while break up means ending the romantic relationship. Contrast: cool off vs cool down — both can mean become less hot/calm; cool down is often more neutral/physical, while cool off often fits anger and can also suggest a temporary relationship pause.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0107 | searches: cool off meaning
