501	5004	5496	freak	/friːk/	noun, informal, often insulting	A person regarded as extremely strange, abnormal, or outside accepted social norms.	weirdo, oddball	The students who didn't fit in were dismissed as freaks.	Can be strongly insulting, though it is sometimes reclaimed or used playfully. 'Freaks and geeks' evokes classic school-outsider categories.		Supplemental from approved batch 4662–4711
501	5005	5411	streak	/striːk/	noun	A long thin line or stripe; a continuous run of similar results or events; or a noticeable tendency in someone's character.	stripe, run, tendency	She has a rebellious streak. / The team is on a winning streak.	Three high-value senses: literal line/stripe; a run such as a winning/losing streak; and a personality tendency such as a stubborn/rebellious streak.		voca_0099–0109 | reviewed improved card
501	5006	5222	be divorced from something (figurative: vocabulary / language)	/biː dɪˈvɔːrst frəm/	figurative phrase	To be so separated from the real context in which something belongs or functions that it loses part of its practical meaning, relevance, or connection to reality. In vocabulary/language learning, it describes words being treated as isolated definitions rather than as language tied to situations, relationships, tone, purpose, and actual use.	be detached from, be disconnected from, be isolated from, be cut off from	Vocabulary can become divorced from context when words are taught as isolated definitions rather than as things people actually say in real situations.	The literal marital sense of divorced is basic and secondary here. The important learning point is the figurative pattern 'X is/becomes divorced from Y,' meaning that X has been separated from something that normally gives it context, grounding, relevance, or meaning. With vocabulary, the phrase criticizes learning or analyzing words in isolation: a word may be memorized as a definition yet be divorced from the situations, collocations, tone, speaker relationships, communicative purpose, and lived experience that make the word natural and usable. Common figurative combinations include divorced from context, reality, practice, experience, meaning, and everyday life. Raw search: 'vocabulary is divorced.'		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0101 | searches: vocabulary is divorced
501	5007	4495	in a vacuum	/ɪn ə ˈvæk.juːm/	idiom	In isolation, without considering the surrounding context, influences, information, or consequences.	in isolation, out of context	You can't evaluate that decision in a vacuum.	Usually figurative in discussion and analysis; literal vacuum has a separate physical meaning.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0099, voca_0107 | searches: in a vacuum meaning
501	5008	4843	queue something up	/kjuː ˈsʌm.θɪŋ ʌp/	phrasal verb	To arrange something to happen, play, or be processed next or in sequence.	line up, schedule, prepare	Queue up the next episode while I make coffee.	Common for music/video, computing tasks, downloads, jobs, and planned actions.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0100 | searches: queue up something meaning
501	5009	3934	biff	/bɪf/	noun / verb (informal)	A hard hit or punch; to hit or punch someone or something.	hit, punch, whack	He biffed the ball straight into the fence.	Comic-book-like and informal; can also appear as a stylized impact sound.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0104 | searches: Biff
501	5010	4774	plaster	/ˈplæs.tɚ/	noun; verb	A material spread on walls/ceilings; BrE, an adhesive bandage; as a verb, to cover a surface heavily or attach something all over it.	coat, cover	Posters were plastered all over the walls.	Useful figurative/passive pattern: be plastered with posters/images.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0108 | searches: plaster
502	5011	4723	oscillation	/ˌɑː.səˈleɪ.ʃən/	noun	A repeated movement or variation back and forth between positions, values, states, or extremes.	fluctuation, vibration, swing	The graph shows rapid oscillations in temperature.	Used literally in physics/engineering and figuratively for repeated shifts in mood, policy, opinion, etc. Verb: oscillate.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0108 | searches: oscillations
502	5012	4475	I'm game	/aɪm ɡeɪm/	informal expression	I am willing and interested in doing the suggested activity.	I'm up for it, count me in, I'm willing	Want to try the new place tonight? I'm game.	Game here is an adjective meaning willing to participate, not the noun meaning a contest.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0109 | searches: i'm game meaing
502	5013	5478	belle	/bel/	noun, somewhat old-fashioned/literary	A beautiful or attractive young woman who is especially admired or socially prominent in a particular place or occasion.	beauty, admired young woman	She was the belle of the ball.	Classic pattern: the belle of the ball. Also possible: a Southern belle, the belle of the town/school. The word carries an older-fashioned social/cultural flavor rather than sounding like ordinary modern 'popular girl.'		Supplemental from approved batch 4662–4711
502	5014	5290	you're (kind of) a lot of work	/jʊr ə lɑːt əv wɝːk/	informal expression	You're demanding, complicated, emotionally taxing, or require a lot of effort, patience, attention, or management from other people.	high-maintenance, demanding, exhausting	I like you, but you're kind of a lot of work sometimes.	'A lot of work' can be teasing/affectionate or genuinely critical. 'Kind of' softens the judgment. It describes the effort involved in dealing with someone, not their work ethic.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0107, voca_0108 | searches: you're kind of a lot of work meaning
502	5015	5345	matrix	/ˈmeɪ.trɪks/	noun	A rectangular array of numbers or symbols in mathematics; more broadly, a surrounding structure, medium, or framework in which something exists, develops, or is embedded.	array, framework, medium, surrounding structure	The data are stored in a matrix. / The cells grow within a protein matrix.	Major senses: mathematics/computing = rectangular array; biology/materials = surrounding substance or structure; figurative = an environment/framework from which something develops. Plural can be 'matrices' /ˈmeɪtrɪsiːz/ or, less formally in some contexts, 'matrixes.'		voca_0099–0109 | reviewed improved card
502	5016	4255	exorcist	/ˈek.sɔːr.sɪst/	noun	A person who performs an exorcism, attempting to expel an evil spirit or supposed supernatural entity.	priest performing an exorcism	The story follows an exorcist called to a remote village.	Related: exorcism, exorcise.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0100 | searches: exorcist meaning
502	5017	4357	get up outta there	/ɡet ʌp ˈaʊt.ə ðer/	informal/slang phrase	To leave a place or situation right away, often with urgency or emphasis.	get out of there, leave, get away	If things start getting weird, just get up outta there.	Also heard/written as get up out of there or get up out there. In informal speech, especially in AAVE-influenced usage, get up out can function as an emphatic leave/go construction. It can also be used figuratively or motivationally for leaving a bad relationship, toxic environment, or other undesirable situation.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0103 | searches: get up out there meaning\
502	5018	4929	sad dad rock	/ˌsæd ˈdæd rɑːk/	noun, informal music label	A humorous, loosely defined label for introspective, melancholy rock/indie music associated with aging or middle-aged male listeners or artists, often emphasizing nostalgia, regret, emotional vulnerability, and subdued instrumentation.	melancholy indie rock, dad rock	The National is frequently described as sad dad rock.	Not a sharply defined genre; often joking or self-aware. Associations commonly include The National, Wilco, The War on Drugs, Elliott Smith and similar introspective indie/alternative rock.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0107 | searches: sad dad rock
502	5019	4034	chieftain	/ˈtʃiːf.tən/	noun	A leader or chief of a people, clan, tribe, or group, especially in historical contexts.	chief, leader	The clans gathered under a powerful chieftain.	Often historical or anthropological. Can sound archaic outside those contexts.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0108 | searches: chieftain
502	5020	5490	misfit	/ˈmɪs.fɪt/	noun	A person who does not fit comfortably into a particular group, environment, or social norm.	outsider, nonconformist	The story follows a group of misfits who become close friends.	Often sympathetic: emphasizes not fitting in rather than being inferior. Common phrase: a band/group of misfits.		Supplemental from approved batch 4662–4711
503	5021	4132	demineralization	/diːˌmɪn.ər.ə.ləˈzeɪ.ʃən/	noun	The loss or removal of minerals from tissue, material, water, or another substance.	mineral loss	Tooth demineralization can occur when acids dissolve minerals from enamel.	Common in dentistry, bone health, water treatment, and materials science.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0107 | searches: demineralization
503	5022	5462	humility	/hjuːˈmɪl.ə.t̬i/	noun	The quality of having a modest and realistic view of one's own importance, abilities, or achievements, including a willingness to admit limits, mistakes, or what one does not know.	modesty, humbleness, lack of arrogance	"Good leadership requires confidence, but also enough humility to admit when you're wrong.
She accepted the praise with humility rather than acting superior."	Deep-dive card. Humility is not weakness, passivity, humiliation, or low self-esteem. It means not placing yourself above others and being able to recognize your own limits without denying your strengths. Contrast humanity = humankind / the human condition / compassion or humaneness. Related adjective: humble.		Supplemental deep-dive card created from batch 3862–3911; paired conceptually with Guidance #3897 humanity.
503	5023	4423	a head-turner	/ə ˈhedˌtɝː.nɚ/	noun, informal	A person or thing so attractive or striking that people turn to look.	stunner, knockout, eye-catcher	That vintage car is a real head-turner.	Can describe people of any gender, as well as cars, clothes, designs, etc.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0109 | searches: head turner girl meaning
503	5024	5149	be touted for/as something		verb phrase	To be publicly praised, promoted, or presented as a strong candidate for a role, award, benefit, or quality.	be promoted as/for, be hailed as, be billed as, be tipped for, be talked up as	The series was touted for its ambitious animation.	Also touted as the next big thing; touted to win can occur.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0107 | searches: define touted for
503	5025	4752	a patronizing look / expression	/ə ˈpeɪ.trəˌnaɪ.zɪŋ lʊk/	noun phrase	A facial expression that conveys condescension, smug sympathy, or an assumption of superiority toward another person.	condescending look, smug expression	He gave me a patronizing look and explained the obvious.	'Patronizing face' is understandable but not a fixed phrase; patronizing look/expression is more idiomatic and reusable.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0104 | searches: patronizing face meaning
503	5026	4823	prudish	/ˈpruː.dɪʃ/	adjective, disapproving	Excessively concerned with sexual propriety or easily shocked by sexual or supposedly improper matters.	prim, strait-laced, puritanical	The network was criticized for its prudish standards.	Adjective corresponding to prude; usually carries a negative judgment.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0107 | searches: define prudish
503	5027	4395	gruff	/ɡrʌf/	adjective	Rough, low, or harsh in voice or manner, often without necessarily being unfriendly.	rough, brusque, gravelly	He has a gruff voice but a kind personality.	Useful contrast: gruff can sound unfriendly while the person may actually be warm.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0099 | searches: gruff meaning
503	5028	5318	systematically / one by one / leave no stone unturned (虱潰しに)		translation / nuance	To check, search, examine, or deal with every possibility or item thoroughly and methodically, one by one, leaving nothing unchecked.	systematically, exhaustively, one by one, leave no stone unturned	We went through the files one by one until we found the missing record.	虱潰しに often describes exhaustive, item-by-item searching/checking. 'Systematically' is neutral; 'one by one' highlights sequence; 'exhaustively' highlights completeness; 'leave no stone unturned' is idiomatic and emphasizes trying every possible avenue, though it is not literally the same image.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0108 | searches: 虱潰しに 英語
503	5029	4942	school belle / the belle of the school	/skuːl bel/	noun phrase, somewhat old-fashioned/literary	An attractive, admired, or socially prominent young woman at a school; roughly, the school's 'belle' or a girl regarded as one of its beauties/social stars.	school beauty, popular girl, campus beauty	She was remembered as the belle of the school.	Usually written as two words: school belle. Belle means a beautiful or admired young woman, especially one prominent in a particular social setting. Compare the classic phrase 'the belle of the ball.' It can evoke an older social world in which a young woman is known for beauty, popularity, or social prominence. Schoolbelles (capitalized, one word) is also a long-established American company that manufactures and sells school uniforms and accessories; the company says it has been in business since 1956 and operates its own sewing factory in Cleveland, Ohio.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0109 | searches: schoolbelle
503	5030	4727	overclock	/ˌoʊ.vɚˈklɑːk/	verb, computing	To run a computer processor or other hardware component at a clock speed higher than its officially rated setting, usually to increase performance.	increase clock speed, tune for performance	He overclocked the CPU to improve gaming performance.	Overclocking can increase heat, power use, and instability. Opposite concept: underclocking.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0101 | searches: overclocking meaning
504	5031	4975	showdown	/ˈʃoʊ.daʊn/	noun	A decisive confrontation, contest, or final test that settles a dispute or determines a winner.	confrontation, face-off	The two candidates are heading for a final showdown.	Originally strongly associated with Western/gunfight imagery; now broad.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0100 | searches: define showdown
504	5032	5138	to the nth degree		idiom	To the greatest or an extreme degree; as far as possible.	to the extreme, to the utmost, to the highest degree, excessively	The production is polished to the nth degree.	Often emphasizes something carried very far.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0101 | searches: to the nth degree
