506	5052	4637	meniscus	/məˈnɪs.kəs/	noun	A curved surface of liquid in a container; in anatomy, a crescent-shaped pad of cartilage in a joint, especially the knee.	curved liquid surface; knee cartilage	Read the volume at the bottom of the meniscus.	Two important senses: laboratory measurement and anatomy. Plural: menisci /məˈnɪs.aɪ/.		voca_0099–0109 | unmatched | folders: voca_0104 | searches: meniscus meaning
